  "issue_title": "[bug] multiply_subspace: compress(B) under-budgets live Atil (m*m) \u2014 OOM gap on static free-memory backends",
  "issue_body": "\ufeff## Summary\n\n`multiply_subspace` keeps `Atil = compress(A, \u2026)` device-resident while calling `compress(B, \u2026)`. The second `compress` sizes its streamed block for `Q + acc + product` only \u2014 it does **not** charge the live `(m, m)` `Atil`.\n\nOn MPS (and any backend where `free_compute_bytes()` is a static ceiling), that under-budgets by `m*m*item`, so the chosen B-compression block can exceed `vram_fraction` and OOM.\n\n## Why distinct\n\n- #266 drops `Atil`/`Btil` **before reconstruct** \u2014 different stage\n- #220/#236 budget compress's own acc/product/Q \u2014 not a *caller-resident* prior compress result\n- `stream_gemm_*` already take `extra_fixed_bytes` for this exact pattern; `compress` never got the parameter\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd `extra_fixed_bytes` to `compress` (mirroring `stream_gemm_*`) and pass `m*m*item` for the B compression while `Atil` is live.\n\nOpen zone: `strategy/` only.\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-17T21:27:12.000Z",
